    "text": "Where a Polling Unit has more than 1,250 voters, such number of registered voters above the specified threshold determined by the Commission, more than one BVAS may be deployed for accreditation. a) The Commission shall publish the list of Polling Units where multiple BVAS will be deployed not later than 14 days before election day and shall make this information available through: I. The Commission's Official website, I. The Commission's State Offices and the Federal Capital Territory (FCT) Office, HN. The Commission's Local Government Area (LGA) Area Council Offices, IV. Stakeholders during the Stakeholders meetings preceding the election, and; V. The affected Polling Unit(s) on the Day of the Election. b) Voters shall be assigned to each BVAS using the first alphabet of their surnames, or in any manner determined by the Commission for that election. The Commission shall display the list of the register of voters as assigned to each BVAS at the affected Polling Unit on the Day of Election. There shall be one Presiding Officer for the Polling Unit notwithstanding the number of BVAS deployed, however, the Commission may appoint additional Assistant Presiding Officers (APOs) to undertake additional functions to facilitate accreditation and voting. The Presiding Officer shall, on conclusion of accreditation, voting and counting of ballot papers: i. Request for all the BVAS used for accreditation in the Polling Unit, ii. Add all the number of accredited voters in all the deployed BVAS together, iii. Record the total accredited voters in the Form EC8A Series and the e-EC8Ain the BVAS, and; iv. There shall be only one result sheet (Form EC8A series) for the Polling Unit irrespective of the number of BVAS deployed and shall be the result to be transmitted to the IRev Portal.",
